# Shell scripts must keep LF on every platform: a CRLF byte at the end of a line
# makes bash read `set -euo pipefail\r` and abort with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name" — exactly how the restore rehearsal failed
# on the server after the code was packaged on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Container and CI definitions are read verbatim.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# SQL migrations are checksummed into the ledger. Keep them LF so a Windows and a
# Linux checkout produce identical bytes.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Presentation packages and rendered media must preserve their exact bytes.
*.pptx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
